  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 602.36 Mean lower low water",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 602.36 “Mean lower low water” means the average of the lower low water height of each tidal day observed over the NTDE, or over an equivalent datum derived for stations with shorter series by comparison of simultaneous observations with a control tide station.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
